# Licences

This repository holds two kinds of material under two different
licences. Which one applies depends on the folder.

## The law text: `corpus/`

Everything under `corpus/` is derived from Commonwealth legislative
instruments published on the Federal Register of Legislation, which
makes them available under the
[Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
(CC BY 4.0).

The Register requires attribution in a set form. Because this
repository changes the presentation of the material, the required form
is the one for changed content:

> Based on content from the Federal Register of Legislation at
> 31 October 2026. For the latest information on Australian Government
> legislation please go to https://www.legislation.gov.au.

Source: the Federal Register of Legislation, https://www.legislation.gov.au.
Each instrument's own page on the Register is linked from
[`corpus.json`](corpus.json) and named in every commit message by its
compilation identifier.

The Commonwealth Coat of Arms is not covered by the CC BY licence and
does not appear here; neither does any material the Register marks as
third-party copyright.

### Changes made

Required by the licence, and listed in full so a reader can judge what
has been done to the text:

1. **Format.** Converted from the Register's Word (`.docx`) files to
   Markdown, one file per provision, with headings as `#` and `##`
   lines. No HTML, fonts, page layout, pagination or styling survives.
2. **Splitting.** Each instrument is split into one file per section,
   regulation or schedule clause, named by its number. Where a Part,
   Division or Schedule carries law text with no provision heading
   beneath it -- the notification forms in the merger determinations are
   whole Divisions written that way -- that text is filed under the
   containers that hold it, as `part-6/div-2.md`. A Schedule written as a
   flat run of numbered items, such as Schedule 13 of the Corporations
   Regulations with its 45 items, is one file for the whole Schedule
   (`sch-13.md`) rather than one per item, because the item numbers
   carry no heading in the source. Every item is in it, in source order.
   The file names are this repository's, not the Register's.
3. **Provisions the source numbers alike.** The 2001 compilation of the
   Corporations Regulations heads two consecutive regulations 5.2.01
   ("Controller's notice to owner or lessor of property -- how given" and
   "Certified copies of reports"); later compilations number the second
   5.2.02. The number is left exactly as that compilation prints it and
   both regulations are kept, in print order, in the file their shared
   number names. Nothing is renumbered. A Schedule whose text runs past
   the end of a volume is joined to its continuation in the next volume.
4. **Characters.** Soft hyphens and zero-width characters are removed.
   The non-breaking hyphen (U+2011) becomes an ordinary hyphen, and the
   non-breaking and thin spaces become ordinary spaces.
5. **Whitespace.** Runs of whitespace are collapsed to one space, and
   each paragraph becomes one line. Tabs that indented paragraph
   numbering are therefore gone.
6. **Tables.** Each row becomes one line, with cells separated by
   ` | `. Merged cells, borders and column widths are not represented.
7. **Omitted.** The table of contents, running page headers and footers,
   and the Register's endnotes (about the endnotes, abbreviation key,
   legislation history, amendment history) are not included. The
   endnotes are the Register's editorial apparatus rather than the law,
   and the same information is carried here by the commit history. The
   compilation's own "About this compilation" front matter is kept, in
   `intro.md`, and it refers to endnotes that are therefore not here;
   read them on the Register, or read the commit history instead.
8. **History.** The commits, their dates and their authorship are
   reconstructed by this repository's tooling from the Register's
   version records. They are not part of the Register's published
   material.

**No word of the legislative text has been added, removed or altered.**
That claim is tested rather than asserted: see
[REPRODUCE.md](REPRODUCE.md).

This repository is not endorsed by the Office of Parliamentary Counsel
or the Commonwealth of Australia.

### Not a substitute for the Register

The Register is authoritative; this is a derived copy, and a compiled
instrument is not the whole law in any event. Use it to find and track
provisions, and read the Register before relying on the words.

